  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi! How are you today?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.61,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm well, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.87,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_25"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Is it actually cheaper to buy in bulk?",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.23,
   "block": "shopping.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Often, yes, but only for things you'll use before they go bad. Toilet paper, rice and canned goods are safe bets.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.36,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "shopping.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "What about fresh stuff?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "block": "shopping.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That's where people waste money. A huge bag of spinach is no deal if half of it wilts.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.32,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "shopping.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Fair. I live alone, so maybe bulk",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 1.04,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "shopping.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "isn't really for me.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.57,
   "block": "shopping.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It can still work. Split a bulk order with a friend or neighbor, or stick to things that freeze well.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.72,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "shopping.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hold on a sec, like what?",
